px 0px 50px 0px","blocks":[{"type":"columns","cols":[{"width":50,"background":"var( --e-global-color-d077a13 )","padding":"30px 0px 30px 0px","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"text":"Vehicle Wrap Warranty Explained: 3M MCS, Avery Dennison ICS and the Installer''s Promise","style":"text-align:center;font-family:\"Poppins\", Sans-serif;font-size:35px;line-height:1.2em;color:#FFFFFF","box":"padding:0px 20px 0px 20px"}]},{"width":50,"blocks":[{"type":"image","src":"/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Paint-Pro-Commercial-Fleet-Wrap-by-Vinyl-Wrap-Toronto-Chevy-Express-and-Dodge-Caravan-Custom-Wraps.webp","alt":"Printed fleet wraps on a Chevrolet Express and Dodge Caravan covered by a manufacturer vehicle wrap warranty programme","full":true}]}]}]},{"id":null,"background":"#FFFFFF","padding":"0px 0px 40px 0px","blocks":[{"type":"columns","cols":[{"width":74.87,"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>\"It comes with a warranty\" is one of the least informative sentences in the wrap business, because three different warranties can be in play on one vehicle and they cover three different things. A <strong>vehicle wrap warranty</strong> might mean the film manufacturer''s basic promise that the roll was not defective, a finished-graphic programme such as 3M''s MCS Warranty or Avery Dennison''s ICS Performance Guarantee, or the installer''s own promise about workmanship. This guide separates the three, explains what each actually covers and excludes, and lists the questions that get you a straight answer before you sign.</p>\n\n<h2>Layer One: The Manufacturer''s Product Warranty</h2>\n<p>The first layer of any vehicle wrap warranty is the one that comes with the roll. Every roll of 3M or Avery Dennison film carries a basic product warranty. 3M''s product bulletins state it the same way each time: the product is warranted to meet 3M''s specifications at the time it ships. If a roll is defective, the remedy is replacement of the product or a refund of its price. It is a warranty on the